[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
IMPLEMENTATION items record concrete mechanisms present in the current source
tree. The statements describe the code as written, including deliberately
unfinished target ports and the current verification boundary. Code references
are recorded as File relations and, where useful, repeated in comments for
readability. These records are descriptive implementation notes rather than
additional behavioral requirements.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Build, configuration, and common failure handling

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-IMP-001
TITLE: Configuration defaults and compile-time guards
STATEMENT: >>>
``include/zef_config.h`` supplies defaults for reactor slots, topic count,
message-pool count, state depth, mailbox capacity, tick type, pool alignment,
assertion mode, claim-counter type, and execution model. ``ZEF_ENABLE_ASSERTIONS``
defaults to enabled and controls only ``ZEF_REQUIRE`` precondition checks;
direct ``ZEF_PANIC`` calls for runtime consistency and resource conditions
remain active. The CMake option with the same name exposes this switch for
complete builds. When disabled, invalid caller inputs are outside the API
contract. Preprocessor checks constrain the configured ranges and execution-
model values. Cooperative mode is the default; preemptive mode is a complete-
build choice for a target Port.
Static assertions check the alignment and the selected integer widths.
``ZefMaxAlign`` provides the maximum scalar alignment used by the default pool
alignment expression on the supported host compilers.
<<<
