[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-IMP-003
TITLE: Panic boundary and ordinary results
STATEMENT: >>>
``ZResult``, ``ZPanicReason``, and ``ZPanicInfo`` are declared in
``include/zef.h``. Fatal framework checks use ``ZEF_PANIC`` directly or
``ZEF_REQUIRE`` for conditional checks; both capture the framework source
location before calling the externally supplied non-returning ``z_panic``
function. The library does not provide a default panic implementation; the
host smoke test supplies an aborting handler. Expected empty, not-running, and
not-found observations use ``ZResult`` while invalid arguments, lifecycle
violations, ownership failures, resource exhaustion, and state errors route
through the panic boundary.
<<<
