[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-IMP-020
TITLE: Descriptor-based Machine
STATEMENT: >>>
State descriptors remain caller-owned ``ZStateNode`` objects containing parent,
initial, handler, enter, and leave links. ``ZMachine`` stores the root, current
node, application context, and lifecycle flags. Dispatch walks parent links
until a handler handles the Message or requests a transition. Transition code
uses fixed-size local path arrays bounded by ``Z_MAX_STATE_DEPTH`` and invokes
leave hooks from the source toward the common ancestor, then enter hooks toward
the target.
<<<
