[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-IMP-030
TITLE: Permanent Reactor registry and lifecycle
STATEMENT: >>>
``src/zef_kernel.c`` assigns each initialized Reactor an explicit zero-based
slot in the Kernel registry. The slot is also the Reactor's strict priority;
the high-water registry bound allows temporary gaps. Registration attaches the
Reactor Mailbox to the Kernel, and start marks the Reactor active and starts
its primary Machine. Registered Reactors remain in the registry for the Kernel
lifetime. The source tree contains no Reactor stop, removal, cleanup, or
terminated-stack path.
<<<
