[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Kernel, topics, and time

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-IMP-040
TITLE: Cooperative Kernel runnable bitmap
STATEMENT: >>>
The Kernel stores one 32-bit runnable bitmap indexed by explicit zero-based
Reactor identity. Reactor identity is also strict priority, with larger
identities running first; unregistered identities may be gaps. Mailbox changes
set or clear a Reactor bit when its primary Reactor is started.
``z_kernel_run_one`` scans runnable identities from high to low, takes one
Message, dispatches the primary Machine, releases the dispatch claim, and
refreshes the bit.
``z_kernel_run_forever`` calls the Port idle callback after a no-work result.
<<<
COMMENT: Code references: include/zef.h; src/zef_kernel.c.
