[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Ports, optional preemption, and verification

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-IMP-070
TITLE: Port callback boundary
STATEMENT: >>>
The target port supplies global ``z_port_critical_enter`` and
``z_port_critical_leave`` operations for processor-wide interrupt exclusion.
``ZPort`` is a public callback structure containing only the Kernel-specific
reschedule request and idle operations. Kernel, TopicTable, Mailbox, and
Message-pool code use the global critical operations; unregistered Mailboxes
and standalone Message pools are therefore protected as well. The generic
library supplies a no-op host default, while a target port overrides the
critical functions with strong definitions.
<<<
