[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-IMP-071
TITLE: Cortex-M0 shared-stack port plan
STATEMENT: >>>
The initial Cortex-M0/M0+ Port source now provides global PRIMASK critical sections,
PendSV rescheduling, WFI idle, and shared-stack exception entry and return.
Target startup/vector integration and hardware validation remain later-phase
work. The selected design is a shared-stack activation port: Reactor handlers
execute on one MSP stack, higher-priority ready Reactors nest through deferred
exception activation, and no Reactor receives process-stack storage. The
the scheduler-only ``ZPort`` callback shape remains the target-neutral boundary; target
exception entry and return are private port implementation details.
<<<
COMMENT: Code references: ``ports/arm-cm0p/zef_arm_cm0p_port.c`` and ``ports/arm-cm0p/zef_arm_cm0p_port.h``. Startup, vector, linker-stack, and hardware validation work remains.
