[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-IMP-074
TITLE: Shared-stack target assembly boundary
STATEMENT: >>>
The Cortex-M0/M0+ port shall use a naked PendSV entry to defer activation
until the last nested interrupt exits, synthesize a valid exception frame to
enter the Kernel activation routine in Thread mode, and use an NMI or reserved
IRQ return path to resume the interrupted shared-stack activation. The port
shall use ``PRIMASK`` rather than ``BASEPRI`` and shall preserve the Armv6-M
exception-frame alignment and Thumb-state requirements.
<<<
COMMENT: The exception boundary is implemented in ``ports/arm-cm0p/zef_arm_cm0p_port.c``; target startup integration and hardware validation are not yet complete.
